{"name":"Adventure of the Seas","hex":"#3063af","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"adventure","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A feeling of desire for new and exciting things.","A remarkable occurrence; a striking event."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To risk oneself. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To risk oneself; to dare to go somewhere or undertake something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adventure"},{"term":"seas","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of sea"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seas"}],"entries":[{"title":"Adventure of the Seas","blocks":[{"text":"Adventure of the Seas is a Voyager-class cruise ship operated by Royal Caribbean International. The vessel was launched and entered service in 2001. Registered in the Bahamas, Adventure of the Seas has cruised from ports in the United States and Europe to sites in the Caribbean Sea, Baltic Sea, Mediterranean Sea, Canada and Europe. The ship has a 138,193 gross tonnage (GT) and is 311.1 meters long with capacity for 3,807 guests."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Adventure_of_the_Seas_at_Grand_Turk.jpg/330px-Adventure_of_the_Seas_at_Grand_Turk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adventure_of_the_Seas","wikidata":"Q379973"},{"title":"Adventure","blocks":[{"text":"An adventure is a novel and exciting undertaking that is typically bold, sometimes risky. Adventures may be activities with danger such as traveling, exploring, skydiving, mountain climbing, scuba diving, river rafting, other extreme sports, or, importantly, any other activity that may be new, fresh or difficult and may even lead to failure. Adventure can take many forms beyond the typically described outdoor area. Adventures are often undertaken to create psychological arousal or in order to achieve a greater goal, such as the pursuit of knowledge that can only be obtained by such activities."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adventure","wikidata":"Q1436734"},{"title":"List of seas on Earth","blocks":[{"text":"This is a list of seas of the World Ocean, including marginal seas, areas of water, various gulfs, bights, bays, and straits. In many cases it is a matter of tradition for a body of water to be named a sea or a bay, etc., therefore all these types are listed here. Entities called \"seas\" which are not divisions of the World Ocean are not included in this list, nor are ocean gyres."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Oceans_and_seas_boundaries_map-en.svg/330px-Oceans_and_seas_boundaries_map-en.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_seas_on_Earth","wikidata":"Q229088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Adventure_of_the_Seas_approaches_Barbados_%282008%29.jpg/500px-Adventure_of_the_Seas_approaches_Barbados_%282008%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Adventure_of_the_Seas_approaches_Barbados_%282008%29.jpg/500px-Adventure_of_the_Seas_approaches_Barbados_%282008%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Adventure of the Seas approaching Barbados on 13 May 2008","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAdventure_of_the_Seas_approaches_Barbados_(2008).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Adventure_of_the_Seas_Wade_2012.JPG/500px-Adventure_of_the_Seas_Wade_2012.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Adventure_of_the_Seas_Wade_2012.JPG/1280px-Adventure_of_the_Seas_Wade_2012.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x